From 6e6b3b07e1ac4be5875465ed531d6e8f169978e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zonglvye <zonglvye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:21:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 85/90] feat(qishui): register the provider and let its CDN
 play directly

Brings upstream's ten provider files over and adapts them to this branch's
contract, which is a 0.7.20 shape rather than 0.7.22's:

- transport: the renderer->main IPC boundary becomes the in-page bridge
  (requestQishuiBridge); scene artwork now goes through the shell proxy because
  douyinpic.com sends no CORS headers
- auth: mapped onto this branch's QR names (getQrKey/createQr/checkQr/cancelQr/
  getQrTtlMs/getQrLoginDiagnostics); describeLoginFailure/getLoginTexts/
  signInRanOut have no counterpart here and are dropped
- library: getLikedSongIds returns the id list (this branch's shape) instead of
  { ids, whole }; the flag is logged until the incremental cache is ported
- recommendations: getPersonalFmCatalog has no hook in this branch's contract, so
  the scene list is an internal cache feeding getRecommendedCollections and
  getPersonalFm
- explore and the failure descriptor are left out (no OnlineExploreProvider /
  OnlineFailureDetail on this branch), as is the provider 'mark'
- types: audioQualityLevels is now an optional part of OnlinePlaybackProvider, so
  a provider can say which qualities it can actually hand out
- shellOnlineAudio: ByteDance CDN hosts bypass the shell relay. Measured on the
  device: ArkWeb's media stack plays the m4a directly and issues its own Range
  requests, so relaying a 1-2 MB file through shell memory only adds a hop.
